{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "GEN",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus the heavens and the earth were finished, and all the host of them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God blessed the seventh day, and sanctified it: because that in it he had rested from all his work which God created and made.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the generations of the heavens and of the earth when they were created, in the day that the LORD God made the earth and the heavens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And every plant of the field before it was in the earth, and every herb of the field before it grew: for the LORD God had not caused it to rain on the earth, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not a man to till the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But there went up a mist from the earth, and watered the whole face of the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD God formed man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD God planted a garden eastward in Eden; and there he put the man whom he had formed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And out of the ground made the LORD God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And a river went out of Eden to water the garden: and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The name of the first ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Pison, which compasseth the whole land of Havilah, where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gold;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the gold of that land ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good: there ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bdellium and the onyx-stone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the name of the second river ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Gihon: the same that compasseth the whole land of Cush.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the name of the third river ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Hiddekel: which floweth toward the east of Assyria. And the fourth river ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Euphrates.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden, to dress it, and to keep it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest of it thou shalt surely die.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD God said, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not good that the man should be alone: I will make him a help meet for him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And out of the ground the LORD God formed every beast of the field, and every fowl of the air, and brought ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Adam to see what he would call them; and whatsoever Adam called every living creature, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " its name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Adam gave names to all cattle, and to the fowls of the air, and to every beast of the field: but for Adam there was not found a help meet for him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD God caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept; and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh in its place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the rib, which the LORD God had taken from man, he made woman, and brought her to the man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Adam said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh: she shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave to his wife: and they shall be one flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.2.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.2.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they were both naked, the man and his wife, and were not ashamed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
